## Recalls keep piling up
As of now, we've crossed a grim milestone: 543 recalls for the year, with 173 of them being classified as Class I recalls, the most severe level. This brings our all-time total to 901 recalls since we started tracking these numbers. Among these, salmonella contamination remains a significant concern, as evidenced by the latest rounds of recalls. 

## The Usual Suspects in the Spotlight
Among the recent recalls, JCB Flavors, LLC has made quite the impression, and not the good kind. With multiple Class I recalls announced on June 10th, their products such as White Cheddar Seasoning and various cheese and garlic toppers have been flagged for potential Salmonella contamination. This has put them squarely in the crosshairs of public scrutiny. 

Straus Family Creamery isn't spared either. Their mint chip and cookie dough premium ice creams have been recalled due to potential metal piece contamination--something no one wants in their dessert.

## The Numbers Don't Lie
The monthly breakdown shows May being particularly bad with 173 recalls, though June seems to be tapering off with 43 recorded so far. The dominance of allergen-related recalls is evident, topping the category chart at 256, followed by Salmonella at 172.

## Final Thoughts
While it's easy to get alarmed by the numbers, it's crucial to stay informed. Check your pantry, review recent purchases, and consult the FDA's website regularly. Companies like JCB Flavors must do better, as trust in food safety is paramount. Stay discerning, stay safe.
